
- **Movement fact:** event-level truth—what happened.
- **Product dimension:** stable descriptive context—what the product is.
- **Product performance mart:** product-level outcomes—how it performs and how often it is returned.

## Return-rate definition 

| Return-rate definition | Formula | Use case |
| ---------------------- | --------| ----------- |
| Unit return rate | returned_units / gross_units_sold | Inventory and merchandising |
| Order return rate | distinct invoices with return / distinct invoices with sale | Customer behavior |
| Value return rate | abs(return signed amount) / gross_sales | Finance |
| Time-boxed return rate | Returns in period / sales from an earlier cohort window | More accurate for delayed returns |

